# A token copy of Arahbo, the First Fang triggers its own "Whenever Arahbo or another nontoken Cat you control enters"
# through "Arahbo" (CR 201.5, 603.6a, 707.2): the token is no nontoken Cat, so only the clause naming itself fires it, and the
# original Arahbo, seeing a token Cat enter, does not trigger. Bot1 casts Arahbo (one Cat token), then Kindle the Inner Flame
# copying her: one more Cat token, not two. The legend rule then keeps one Arahbo (CR 704.5j).
[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus x3
Arahbo, the First Fang
Kindle the Inner Flame
Mountain x2
Mountain x10
[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20
[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Arahbo, the First Fang.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield = Black Lotus; Black Lotus; Arahbo, the First Fang; Cat Token
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Kindle the Inner Flame.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Arahbo, the First Fang)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield = Arahbo, the First Fang; Cat Token; Cat Token

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Arahbo, the First Fang; Cat Token; Cat Token
